The function `__ioam6_fill_trace_data()` in `net/ipv6/ioam6.c` calls `__in6_dev_get()` without checking its return value for NULL. When the device does not have an IPv6 `inet6_dev` structure (e.g., non-IPv6 interfaces or transient states), `__in6_dev_get()` returns NULL, leading to a potential NULL pointer dereference when accessing `cnf.ioam6_id` or `cnf.ioam6_id_wide`.

